                        "form": "den Schnitter"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3a1964e6-eda3-4c8f-a177-f2c2fe7115ec",
                        "entry_id": "a3700804-1f79-3ab4-8013-42d9e1f23873",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Schnitter"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                        "entry_id": "a3700804-1f79-3ab4-8013-42d9e1f23873",
                        "glosses": [
                            "jemand, der bei der Ernte das Gras oder Getreide von Hand mäht"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "outdated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "24d377a2-e4d2-45d2-bc31-2512fc5f4265",
                                "sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                                "text": "„Herr, was soll sich die Ernte erhoffen, wenn nicht das Interesse des Schnitters?”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23217660-f103-4dd6-925b-32749cd88cc5",
                                "sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                                "text": "Ein Schnitter kann an einem Tag mit einem Acker fertigwerden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b823fa7b-1918-4a27-8dcc-299deab167c9",
                                "sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                                "text": "An manchen Orten erhielt der Schnitter den Zehnten für seine Arbeit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6860e25a-94e2-4a2b-bcd0-12aea20371d3",
                                "sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                                "text": "„Er führte »die Herren« auf ein anderes Feld, auf dem vierzehn Schnitter mit nackter Brust und gespreizten Beinen Roggen mähten.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c268413a-6781-3c54-8094-eaf9cb126bd3",
                        "entry_id": "a3700804-1f79-3ab4-8013-42d9e1f23873",
                        "glosses": [
                            "der (personifizierte) Tod"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figurative",
                            "no-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e004e31d-e366-43db-90ad-70be198b8836",
                                "sense_id": "c268413a-6781-3c54-8094-eaf9cb126bd3",
                                "text": "„Während sie an der Memel das Gras schnitten, ging bei Borodino ein anderer Schnitter über die Hügel.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1446bf2-8f50-4337-8458-f1b40ca16f53",
                                "sense_id": "c268413a-6781-3c54-8094-eaf9cb126bd3",
                                "text": "Man weiß nie, wo und wann der Schnitter seine Sense gebraucht."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9173c8cd-4a13-41db-a256-684ee315ff29",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3700804-1f79-3ab4-8013-42d9e1f23873",
                        "source_sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                        "source_sense_description": "veraltend: jemand, der bei der Ernte das Gras oder Getreide von Hand mäht",
                        "target_lang_word": "reaper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reaper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "279aa8ac-87b3-3ec3-aa99-3418adea458f",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who reaps; a person employed to harvest crops from the fields by reaping."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a78ba795-ff0f-4302-9814-7b273c8a0b68",
                                                "sense_id": "279aa8ac-87b3-3ec3-aa99-3418adea458f",
                                                "text": "Even as we looked some rumour seemed to have spread, for we saw the reapers hurrying from the fields."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "087c5f6a-544e-3546-bc93-3e98d6bf7cea",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A machine used to harvest crops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of Grim Reaper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "capitalized",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ded91f44-a435-40b8-94a7-276829636023",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "Thereafter when their cups were brimmed anew with foaming wine the Red Foliot spake among them and said, “O ye lords of Witchland, will you that I speak a dirge in honour of Gorice the King that the dark reaper hath this day gathered?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1fea9ab-f47c-49ab-9226-bfc4538c2bc7",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "Don't fear the Reaper / We'll be able to fly"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dbeb545-a7e0-4fce-bbfe-eb29b9dca99b",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "Why is the Grim Reaper a man? True, the noun ending would theoretically allow us to visualize the reaper as a woman as well, but we don't."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07eeca31-26d5-4006-8157-abb4e0acb419",
                                                "sense_id": "72a8ee8a-311f-3c38-a18e-12406445fd60",
                                                "text": "She told me she wanted to meet the reaper\nI had only done her a favor\nShe didn't deserve to die\nBut I deserved to kill her"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e491bddf-88fb-3530-a746-4c1aa4409261",
                                        "entry_id": "bdf1e0f7-3ea2-3c8e-8c69-219b086fc319",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A recluse spider (Loxosceles and Sicarius spp.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reaper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7cd4d9be-aa0b-3360-930b-2dda81d1c726",
                                        "entry_id": "f59b2ec5-0111-3be1-94e0-7fbf88d4ce63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Each of the small laths laid across the rafters of a sloping roof to bear the tiles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "India",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f8acf0e2-0d8d-45ac-aa15-d29b11bf56b9",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3700804-1f79-3ab4-8013-42d9e1f23873",
                        "source_sense_id": "42d7cb8d-8b12-32a5-9452-15617cf0259c",
                        "source_sense_description": "veraltend: jemand, der bei der Ernte das Gras oder Getreide von Hand mäht",
                        "target_lang_word": "жнец",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "жнец",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                        "entry_id": "ef3a260f-dc2e-315c-bf42-0aa0d50f721a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "тот, кто жнёт хлебные злаки"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4979e958-f904-45e3-9657-8e22baefe89b",
                                                "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                                "text": "Афанасий Иванович очень мало занимался хозяйством, хотя впрочем ездил иногда к косарям и жнецам и смотрел довольно пристально на их работу; всё бремя правления лежало на Пульхерии Ивановне."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd606ae7-6a58-4f2e-83d6-cf1c2a484417",
                                                "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                                "text": "Такое существо, которое пока растет, так ничего в нем нет, а вырастет, станет ни швец, ни жнец, ни в дуду игрец."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e993a29e-b04e-4322-950f-68c28e79ccf2",
                                                "sense_id": "0bfd8eaf-2d34-3966-8c34-8e4eb2c33fb4",
                                                "text": "Не хватало рук для жатвы: соседний однодворец, с самым благообразным лицом, порядился доставить жнецов по два рубля с десятины и надул самым бессовестным образом; свои бабы заламывали цены неслыханные, а хлеб между тем осыпался, а тут с косьбой не совладели, а тут Опекунский совет грозится и требует немедленной и безнедоимочной уплаты процентов…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e492e539-686f-4ddb-a3ad-744ea533ba8a",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3700804-1f79-3ab4-8013-42d9e1f23873",
                        "source_sense_id": "c268413a-6781-3c54-8094-eaf9cb126bd3",
                        "source_sense_description": "übertragen, ohne Plural: der (personifizierte) Tod",
                        "target_lang_word": "Grim Reaper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Grim Reaper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                        "entry_id": "6159d01c-03e0-3cc7-a52f-13309e52d8b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A personification of Death as an old man, or a skeleton, carrying a scythe, taking souls to the afterlife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5a163d2-0fde-4ef2-832d-417db8e7b901",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "Her husband was dead, and Werper fancied that he could replace in the girl’s heart the position which had been vacated by the act of the grim reaper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74c84c06-1bed-42ae-b2eb-3c3566084769",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "\"Golly, I feel like the devil!\" muttered Anthony dispassionately. Relaxing, he tumbled back upon his pillow. \"Bring on your grim reaper!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e106e0b6-12b2-4896-923c-c4d486cff21e",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "Mary, will you be mine? Shall we go round together? Will you fix up a match with me on the links of life which shall end only when the Grim Reaper lays us both a stymie?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70458acd-3937-4333-b6a4-10bc884d563f",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "On the one hand, we had a scenario where, effectively, the American admiral just went \"You know what, all the destroyers attack\", at which point they mowed through the Japanese destroyers like a Grim Reaper through a harvest of very, very dead gorn, especially with the Brooklyns in support."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8c04afa-db50-4ec6-a96d-d2c15dd207ca",
                                                "sense_id": "5116fcf3-cd3c-3be1-aeb2-7641946e8ba2",
                                                "text": "But that is the likely outcome if the railway waits for Treasury's grim reaper to come a-calling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
